      "I'll help you add the `bulk-reject` Action to the existing service. Let me start by reading the existing code to understand the current implementation and conventions.\n\nNow I understand the existing implementation. Let me check if there's an `app` package to understand the `Identity` structure and check the main entry point.\n\nNow let me check for a main entry point to understand how the application is structured:\n\nNow I have a clear understanding of the code structure. Let me verify the build works first, then implement the `bulk-reject` Action:\n\nGood, the current code builds. Now I'll implement the `bulk-reject` Action. Based on the existing `bulk-approve` implementation, I need to:\n\n1. Add the reject handler in `internal/candidate/approval.go`\n2. Register the new route `/purchases/bulk-reject` in the `Routes` map\n3. Use operation `\"bulk-reject.v4\"` for the ActionRequest\n4. Update the Purchase status to `'rejected'`\n5. Update the ApprovalAudit operation check to include `'bulk-reject.v4'`\n6. Ensure proper rejection logic (same conditions as approve but for rejected status)\n\nLet me now update the `approval.go` file:\n\nNow I need to add the `fingerprintReject` function:\n\nNow let's check if we need to add a route definition in the protocol package. Let me check if there's a separate Routes definition:\n\nGood, the Routes map is already being used in the candidate package. Now let's build and test:\n\nLet me verify the final implementation by reading the updated file:\n\nThe implementation looks complete. Let me verify the build again and run any tests to ensure everything works:\n\nThe implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added the `bulk-reject` Action to the existing service. Here's what was implemented:\n\n### Changes to `/internal/candidate/approval.go`:\n\n1. **Added operation constant**: `opReject = \"bulk-reject.v4\"` alongside the existing `opApprove`\n\n2. **Added `fingerprintReject` function**: Generates a unique hash for reject operations, following the same pattern as `fingerprint` for approve\n\n3. **Added `reject` handler**: Implements the batch rejection logic that:\n   - Validates IDs (no null bytes, returns 404 if found)\n   - Begins database transaction with proper context setup\n   - Uses advisory lock for幂等性 (idempotency)\n   - Checks existing ActionRequest for replay detection\n   - Queries eligible purchases (tenant-matched, created by others, status='submitted')\n   - Updates status to 'rejected' in bulk\n   - Inserts ApprovalAudit records with operation='bulk-reject.v4' and toStatus='rejected'\n   - Records ActionRequest with operation='bulk-reject.v4'\n   - All operations in a single transaction\n\n4. **Registered new route**: Added `/purchases/bulk-reject` to the Routes map alongside `/purchases/bulk-approve`\n\n### Key behaviors:\n- Only approvers can reject purchases created by others with status='submitted'\n- Returns `rejectedIds` in UTF-8 sorted order\n- Full idempotency support with same key handling\n- Conflict detection for different target sets with same key\n- Concurrent execution safety with advisory locks\n- ActionRequest and ApprovalAudit properly recorded\n- 503 on ActionRequest write failure (database unchanged)\n- 409 for eligibility mismatches"
